    "headline": "Lamar and Henry vs our 78.9 front, and the No. 1 coverage in the league",
    "bottomLine": "Baltimore is better than the Falcons in six of nine units and ranks 1st in coverage and 3rd in run defense, so there is no easy passing game. The win is the right side of their line: Lindstrom +7.1 on Calais Campbell and Pitts on Trenton Simpson (MCV 62). On defense the game is lost if Lamar (95 SPD) escapes contain or Henry gets free runs at a 78.9 front; keep five DBs, spy, and make them drive it.",
    "identity": {
      "offense": "A two-X-Factor run offense: Lamar (95 SPD, RUN 95) plus Henry (BCV 97, TRK 91) behind Stanley (88.4). The book is heavy on 12/13 personnel sets like Gun Heavy Raven and Pistol Full House TE, with Andrews (CIT 90) as the chain mover. Receivers rank only 16th.",
      "defense": "A top-4 defense built from the back: Hamilton (PRC 95, MCV 87) as a roaming chess piece, three corners at 81 to 85 OVR, Roquan Smith (PUR 97) cleaning up the run, Hendrickson (FMV 94) and Madubuike (TAK 96) the pressure. The soft spots are Zion Young at LEDGE and Simpson at WILL.",
      "expectFromUser": [
        "Scramble Lamar outside the edge on any third down where the first read is covered",
        "Pound Henry in heavy sets until Freight Train is live, then keep feeding him",
        "Throw Andrews over the middle against linebackers, especially our WILL",
        "User Hamilton or Roquan in the middle of the field to take away our dig and seam",
        "Bring Hendrickson off our left side and a DT twist at Bergeron"
      ]
    },
    "keys": [
